          "id": "india-black-mass-export-ban-2026-11-11",
          "headline": "India bans exports of lithium-ion battery 'black mass' with immediate effect",
          "summary": "The DGFT moved spent-battery waste and scrap under HS code 85491400, described as lithium-ion battery black mass, from 'free' to 'prohibited' for export, in a notification dated November 10. Black mass is the powder left after old batteries are crushed; it holds lithium, cobalt, nickel, manganese and graphite. It is not a ban on all battery materials.",
          "why_it_matters": "Keeping black mass at home is meant to feed India's own battery recyclers and secure critical minerals.",
          "importance": 4,
          "lead": false,
          "verified": true,
          "note": null,
